what when was the first time you heard  about West Side Story and how did you  get involved with the production of the  film well we we we joined United Artists  under an arrangement where we would  produce films for them and we  fortunately we we made a few pictures  that I am also very proud of prior to  making West Side Story the first of  which was in the Magnificent Seven which  you you may recall and after that some  like it hot which you will also recall  some what I'm during that period I was  in New York with my wife we decided we  were going to go to the theater and see  a show and we chose West Side Story and  it it just knocked me out it one of the  most extraordinary musicals I had ever  seen on a stage and and I said oh my god  wouldn't it be exciting to make a film  of that and then a long complicated  process began and finally we we were  able to corral the rights to it and well  you'll see the result of it here  this sounds good so I just want to  remind everybody that when this film  came out the the blacklist was your when  that was being made the blacklist was  still alive in Hollywood and the civil  rights movement was just getting started  I mean this was really a very  aggressively modern take on race  relations in America and also to take  the well that was one of the what are  the principal things that that  recommended it to me I thought this was  a an extraordinary opportunity to say  something about racial relations in  America  mm-hm and to say it in a way that would  bring audiences to see it and and  perhaps benefit from the lesson of West  Side Story mm-hmm I as you see it now  and and connect it with the what what's  happening every week now it it is more  topical I think even than it was at that  time and I my efforts in this direction  which also included my film in the heat  of the night which  which I hope would also reach people  with a a certain understanding of the  possibilities of the necessity for the  races to come together and and stop this  senseless warfare it is discouraging  that that lesson has still not been  learned and I hope others will take up  the cudgels and continue to fight that  battle
 

